<odoo>
    <!--
        🔴 NOTHING GOES IN A NEW PLACE, AND THAT IS THE DESIGN RATHER THAN A
        LAYOUT PREFERENCE. The first version of this was a dedicated "Vendor
        Data" tab, and it was rejected on sight: buried in the last tab it
        gets lost, the accountant just searches for a vendor and the data never
        improves. A tab is optional work for somebody with a bill to finish,
        and optional work does not happen.

        So everything here hangs directly under the Vendor field, and there are
        only two things: the candidate list (when there is no vendor) and ONE
        line (when details differ).

        🔴 BEFORE YOU CHANGE ANYTHING IN THIS FILE, TWO THINGS THAT COST A
        SHIPPED DEFECT AND TEN MINUTES OF MISDIAGNOSIS.

        1. **NO SERVER TEST CAN SEE A MODIFIER THAT IS TOO PERMISSIVE.**
           `get_view` returns ONE arch for every record, so an assertion of the
           form *"the arch contains this block"* passes whatever the block's
           `invisible=` says. That is how the unmatched-vendor explanation
           shipped with `invisible="partner_id"` where it needed
           `invisible="partner_id or not ai_from_import"` — and showed *"nothing
           was recognised… or create the contact from what was read off the
           document"* on every bill anyone typed by hand. Found by pressing
           **New** in a browser.
           → Where an element is conditional, the test must EVALUATE its
           modifier against a record of each state. `tests/
           test_unmatched_vendor_ui.py::_element_invisible_for` does that and is
           the helper to reuse. Pixels are still outside any server test, and a
           visual change still needs a browser.

        2. **A `-u` FROM ANOTHER CONTAINER DOES NOT RELOAD PYTHON IN A RUNNING
           SERVER.** After upgrading this module from a side process, loading a
           bill threw `"account.move"."ai_can_create_vendor" field is
           undefined` — which reads exactly like a field missing from the arch,
           and is not. The DATABASE had the new view; the serving process still
           had the old Python in memory and no such field in its registry. The
           module was correct the whole time.
           → After a code change, RESTART the serving process. A view-only
           change travels with the `-u`; a new field, compute or method does
           not.

        ⚠️ NO OWL, NO CUSTOM WIDGET. An inline one2many list with object
        buttons. Two traps in this tree make a widget the wrong bet:
          * 19.0's `evalPartialContext` SILENTLY DROPS any field-`context` key
            whose expression names a record field, because a form's field
            context is evaluated before the record is read — so the move's id
            cannot be passed into the Vendor many2one's own context to rank its
            dropdown. The candidates are shown BESIDE the field instead.
          * a duplicate OWL template name aborts the WHOLE `web.assets_web`
            bundle, silently. A duplicate-template check exists because that
            already happened in another add-on.
    -->

    <record id="view_move_form_vendor_suggestions" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">account.move.form.vendor.suggestions</field>
        <field name="model">account.move</field>
        <field name="inherit_id" ref="account.view_move_form"/>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <!-- Anchored on the widget, which is unique in this form in 19.0
                 (`account/views/account_move_views.xml:1013`). If a later core
                 or another module changes it the inherit FAILS LOUDLY at
                 install, which is the wanted direction: `gate_views.py` exists
                 because an xpath that quietly stops matching leaves the feature
                 absent and everything green. -->
            <xpath expr="//field[@name='partner_id'][@widget='res_partner_many2one']"
                   position="after">
                <field name="ai_vendor_review_deferred" invisible="1"/>
                <field name="ai_from_import" invisible="1"/>
                <field name="ai_can_create_vendor" invisible="1"/>
                <field name="ai_vendor_draft_bill_count" invisible="1"/>

                <!-- Screen 1: the bill has no vendor. The candidates are here,
                     ranked by how many POSTED bills we have had from each,
                     because history is the tiebreak a person actually uses. -->
                <!-- 🔴 A KANBAN, NOT A LIST, AND THAT CHANGED AFTER LOOKING AT
                     IT. The first version was a `<list>` with four columns —
                     Vendor | Why | Bills | Use this — inside a one2many that
                     sits in the form's NARROW left column. Measured in a
                     browser: the reason rendered as "same phone nu…" and the
                     vendor name as "NORTHWIND - Smith r…". That is the one thing
                     the screen cannot afford, because the three candidates on a
                     Northwind bill are NORTHWIND, `NORTHWIND - Smith reps` and
                     `Northwind - Smith Reps` and the clipped part is the part
                     that tells them apart. A list column divides a fixed width;
                     a kanban card does not, so the name wraps instead of being
                     cut and the reason gets a line of its own.
                     ⚠️ STILL NO OWL — `<kanban>` is plain arch, compiled by
                     core. The two traps above apply unchanged.
                     `can_open="false"`: a kanban card opens a form dialog on
                     click by default, and there is no form for this model — the
                     ONLY action a candidate offers is its button. -->
                <!-- 🔴 THE EXPLANATION IS OUTSIDE THE CANDIDATE DIV, AND IT WAS
                     INSIDE IT UNTIL 19.0.3.24.0. On bill B the form showed
                     neither the candidate box nor the offer to create the
                     vendor. The sentence lived inside the block whose
                     `invisible="partner_id or not ai_vendor_candidate_ids"`
                     hides it exactly when the candidate list is EMPTY — so the
                     one bill shape that most needs an explanation rendered a
                     blank area beside the Vendor field. On a database with
                     only a handful of vendors, where every unmatched bill
                     comes from a new carrier, the candidate list is
                     legitimately empty on every one.
                     The chatter said all of this; the form said nothing.

                     Two wordings, because the two cases ask for different
                     things from the reader: with candidates, pick one; without,
                     nothing matched and here is the button. -->
                <!-- 🔴 `not ai_from_import` IS HALF THE CONDITION AND LEAVING
                     IT OUT SHIPPED A LIE ON EVERY HAND-TYPED BILL. Found in a
                     browser, after this block had passed every
                     server test: press New on the Bills list and the blank form
                     said *"This vendor was not recognised and nothing in the
                     contact book came close… or create the contact from what
                     was read off the document"* — on a bill with no document,
                     naming a button that was correctly hidden.

                     The button's own gate already carried `not ai_from_import`;
                     the explanation did not, because when it moved OUT of the
                     candidate div it inherited only the `partner_id` half of
                     that div's condition. The two gates have to agree, and the
                     test that holds them together is
                     `test_the_explanation_is_hidden_on_a_bill_nobody_imported`.

                     ⚠️ SAME SHAPE AS SCREEN 1b BELOW, for the same reason
                     recorded there: a bill typed by a person had its vendor
                     chosen by that person, so there is nothing to explain and
                     the line would be noise on every manual bill in the
                     database. -->
                <!-- 🔴 `groups=` ON THE BLOCK, NOT JUST ON THE FIELD, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT.
                     The fields inside carry `groups="account.group_account_invoice"` because
                     without it a salesperson could not open an invoice at
                     all. But `get_view` strips a restricted FIELD and leaves everything else
                     standing — so the `invisible="not ai_vendor_candidate_ids"` modifiers below
                     would survive, referencing a field that is no longer in the arch, and the
                     client would throw on a name it cannot resolve. One error traded for another.
                     Restricting the container removes the elements and their modifiers together. -->
                <div class="o_ai_vendor_unmatched mb-2"
                     groups="account.group_account_invoice"
                     invisible="partner_id or not ai_from_import">
                    <span class="text-muted"
                          invisible="not ai_vendor_candidate_ids">
                        This vendor was not recognised, so the bill has no vendor.
                        Nothing was invented — pick one, or create the contact:
                    </span>
                    <span class="text-muted"
                          invisible="ai_vendor_candidate_ids">
                        This vendor was not recognised and nothing in the contact
                        book came close, so the bill has no vendor. Nothing was
                        invented — pick a vendor on the field above, or create the
                        contact from what was read off the document:
                    </span>
                    <!-- Item 3: the button the chatter note has been promising
                         since F27 (*"or create one deliberately"*). It is NOT a
                         return to automatic creation — see
                         `account.move.action_ai_create_vendor_from_extraction`
                         for the distinction and for the four things it refuses
                         to do. Shown only on a draft bill that came from the
                         import and still carries a readable extraction; the
                         method re-checks every one of those, because a button's
                         visibility rule is UI only and an RPC is not the UI. -->
                    <div class="mt-1" invisible="not ai_from_import or not ai_can_create_vendor">
                        <button name="action_ai_create_vendor_from_extraction"
                                type="object"
                                string="Create contact from this invoice"
                                class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm"
                                invisible="state != 'draft'"
                                help="Creates one contact from the name, address and tax id read off this document, files the bill against it, and records in the chatter who asked for it. If a matching contact already exists it is used instead, so pressing this twice cannot make two."/>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="o_ai_vendor_candidates mb-2"
                     groups="account.group_account_invoice"
                     invisible="partner_id or not ai_vendor_candidate_ids">
                    <field name="ai_vendor_candidate_ids" nolabel="1"
                           readonly="state != 'draft'"
                           options="{'no_create': True, 'no_open': True}">
                        <!-- `o_ai_vendor_candidate_cards` is the hook for the
                             one rule in `static/src/scss/vendor_candidates.scss`
                             — see there for why a stylesheet is needed at all
                             (core pins the card width to 320 px ON the renderer,
                             so no ancestor and no inline style can win). -->
                        <kanban class="o_ai_vendor_candidate_cards"
                                create="false" delete="false"
                                quick_create="false" can_open="false"
                                records_draggable="false">
                            <field name="sequence"/>
                            <field name="partner_archived"/>
                            <field name="draft_bill_count"/>
                            <templates>
                                <t t-name="card"
                                   class="flex-row align-items-center gap-3">
                                    <div class="flex-grow-1">
                                        <div>
                                            <field name="partner_id" class="fw-bold"/>
                                            <span class="badge text-bg-warning ms-1"
                                                  invisible="not partner_archived">Archived</span>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="text-muted small">
                                            <field name="reason"/>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="text-muted small"
                                             invisible="not partner_location">
                                            <field name="partner_location"/>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <!-- The count large and right-aligned, with
                                         the word under it. The list version had
                                         to abbreviate the header to "Bills" to
                                         fit; here the word is a line of its own
                                         and the number is the thing the eye
                                         lands on, which is how the tiebreak is
                                         meant to be read. -->
                                    <div class="text-end flex-shrink-0">
                                        <div class="fs-5 fw-bold lh-1">
                                            <field name="bill_count"/>
                                        </div>
                                        <!-- ⚠️ "posted", not "bills". This was
                                             the ONE place in the module that
                                             labelled the number without the
                                             word, while the field help, the
                                             form line and the chatter all said
                                             "posted bills" — so a reader could
                                             take it for all bills, which is the
                                             misreading bill D
                                             showed. -->
                                        <div class="text-muted small">posted</div>
                                        <!-- The draft count, under the posted
                                             one and deliberately quieter: a
                                             draft is not evidence this vendor
                                             has been paid before, it is a
                                             reason not to read 0 as "new". -->
                                        <div class="text-muted small lh-1"
                                             invisible="draft_bill_count == 0">
                                            <field name="draft_bill_count"/> draft
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <button name="action_use_this" type="object"
                                            string="Use this"
                                            class="btn btn-primary btn-sm flex-shrink-0"/>
                                </t>
                            </templates>
                        </kanban>
                    </field>
                </div>

                <!-- Screen 1b: the bill HAS a vendor — is it the RIGHT one?
                     The requirement: a number on or beside the vendor name
                     saying how many vendor bills this vendor has, so the user
                     can always be sure this is the right contact.

                     🔴 ZERO IS THE LOUD STATE, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE FEATURE.
                     A vendor with history needs no attention — the number is
                     reassurance and is deliberately plain muted text. A vendor
                     with NONE is either genuinely new or the matcher picking
                     the wrong record out of a book that holds `NORTHWIND`,
                     `NORTHWIND - Smith reps` and `Northwind - Smith Reps`, and
                     that is the only case worth stopping for. So 0 does not
                     render as a grey "0" beside a grey "7" — the shape an eye
                     skims — it renders as an amber line that says it in words.

                     ⚠️ ONLY ON AN IMPORTED BILL (`ai_from_import`). A bill
                     typed by a person had its vendor chosen by that person, so
                     there is nothing to double-check and the line would be
                     noise on every manual bill in the database. The test is one
                     `ai.invoice.import` row pointing at the move; widening this
                     to every vendor bill is deleting `or not ai_from_import`
                     from the line below, if that is wanted later.

                     🔴 `d-flex` ON THE PARENT **AND** `w-auto flex-grow-0
                     flex-shrink-0` ON THE FIELD — the same pair as the alert
                     below, for the same measured reason: a `<field>` renders
                     inside core's `o_field_widget` wrapper, a block Odoo's CSS
                     stretches to the full column (MEASURED at 504 px for a
                     one-character integer in this very module), and `d-flex`
                     alone does not fix it because the wrapper is then a flex
                     item that keeps its width and wraps everything else down. -->
                <div class="o_ai_vendor_bill_history mb-2"
                     invisible="not partner_id or not ai_from_import">
                    <div class="alert alert-warning py-1 px-2 mb-0
                                d-flex align-items-center flex-wrap gap-1"
                         role="status"
                         invisible="ai_vendor_bill_count != 0">
                        <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle"
                           role="img" aria-label="Warning" title="Warning"/>
                        <!-- 🔴 THREE SENTENCES, ONE PER STATE OF THE DRAFT
                             COUNT, AND BILL D IS WHY. A vendor can have no
                             posted and several draft bills, and the
                             one sentence that used to stand here was true in
                             every word while the conclusion a reader draws from
                             it — "nobody has ever bought from this vendor" —
                             was wrong.

                             ⚠️ The drafts are NOT added into the posted number.
                             This alert is still the zero-POSTED state, because
                             "has this vendor ever been paid" is the question it
                             answers; the drafts are a second fact reported
                             beside it. Folding them in would have hidden this
                             amber line on exactly the bills that produced the
                             complaint.

                             QWeb has no plural form and the arch cannot call
                             `_()`, so singular and plural are two spans — the
                             same shape as the posted line below, which used
                             to read "1 posted bills". -->
                        <span invisible="ai_vendor_draft_bill_count != 0">No posted bills from this vendor yet — check this is the right contact.</span>
                        <span invisible="ai_vendor_draft_bill_count != 1">No posted bills from this vendor yet, but there is 1 other draft — check this is the right contact.</span>
                        <span invisible="ai_vendor_draft_bill_count &lt; 2">No posted bills from this vendor yet, but there are</span>
                        <field name="ai_vendor_draft_bill_count" nolabel="1" readonly="1"
                               invisible="ai_vendor_draft_bill_count &lt; 2"
                               class="fw-bold w-auto flex-grow-0 flex-shrink-0"/>
                        <span invisible="ai_vendor_draft_bill_count &lt; 2">other drafts — check this is the right contact.</span>
                    </div>
                    <!-- ⚠️ `align-items-baseline`, NOT `-center`, and `small`
                         repeated ON the field. Looked at: with `center` the
                         field's own 19.5 px box sat at the TOP of the 24.5 px
                         row and the number read as a superscript, because the
                         `<field>` renders at 13 px while the sentence beside it
                         is `.small`. Baselines line up; box centres do not. -->
                    <div class="text-muted small
                                d-flex align-items-baseline flex-wrap gap-1"
                         invisible="ai_vendor_bill_count == 0">
                        <field name="ai_vendor_bill_count" nolabel="1" readonly="1"
                               class="small fw-bold w-auto flex-grow-0 flex-shrink-0"/>
                        <!-- Two spans, not one: QWeb has no plural form and
                             the arch cannot call `_()`. One span used to read
                             "1 posted bills". The wrapper above is already
                             hidden at 0, so these two cover 1 and >1. -->
                        <span invisible="ai_vendor_bill_count != 1">posted bill from this vendor already.</span>
                        <span invisible="ai_vendor_bill_count == 1">posted bills from this vendor already.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Screen 2: ONE line, and only when something differs. The
                     EMPTY fields were already filled and logged; nobody was
                     asked, because filling a blank cannot lose anything. -->
                <!-- 🔴 `d-flex` ON THE ALERT **AND** `w-auto flex-grow-0
                     flex-shrink-0` ON THE FIELD. Both halves were found by
                     looking, and neither is guessable from the arch.
                     A `<field>` renders inside Odoo's own `o_field_widget`
                     wrapper, which is a block that Odoo's CSS stretches to the
                     full column — MEASURED at 504 px for a one-character
                     integer. So the count sat on its own line above the
                     sentence and the notice read as two lines. `d-flex` alone
                     did NOT fix it: the wrapper is a flex item, keeps its
                     width, and `flex-wrap` then pushes everything else down.
                     `w-auto` collapses it to its content (measured: 8.5 px),
                     and the alert becomes one 31 px line.
                     🔴 No server test can see any of this — `get_view` returns
                     the same arch either way. -->
                <div class="o_ai_vendor_conflicts alert alert-info py-1 px-2 mb-2
                            d-flex align-items-center flex-wrap gap-1"
                     role="status"
                     groups="account.group_account_invoice"
                     invisible="ai_vendor_suggestion_count == 0 or ai_vendor_review_deferred">
                    <field name="ai_vendor_suggestion_count" nolabel="1"
                           readonly="1"
                           class="fw-bold w-auto flex-grow-0 flex-shrink-0"/>
                    <span>details on this invoice differ from this vendor.</span>
                    <button name="action_ai_review_vendor_suggestions"
                            type="object" string="Review"
                            class="btn-link p-0 ms-1"/>
                    <button name="action_ai_defer_vendor_suggestions"
                            type="object" string="Not now"
                            class="btn-link p-0"
                            help="Leaves them pending. They go to the vendor-data queue, so this is never the same person's problem twice."/>
                </div>

                <!-- 🔴 RED, AND THE ONLY SIGNAL (19.0.3.31.0). The
                     requirement: the PDF's lines only, and any discrepancy
                     shown as a red banner for a person to review. The bill carries the document's
                     lines and nothing else; this compares the bill's LIVE
                     total and tax with what was printed, so it goes away once
                     the bill is fixed. Tax is mentioned only when the tax
                     differs. It does not block posting.
                     ⚠️ NO `d-flex`: the sentence is longer than the column, so
                     as one flex item it wrapped away from the icon (looked at,
                     19.0.3.29.0). The amounts are `d-inline-block w-auto ms-1`
                     so they sit inside the sentence with a space before them;
                     without `ms-1` the arch's whitespace is lost and it read
                     "is$ 180.90" (looked at, 19.0.3.30.0). -->
                <field name="ai_total_mismatch" invisible="1"/>
                <field name="ai_tax_mismatch" invisible="1"/>
                <div class="o_ai_total_mismatch alert alert-danger py-1 px-2 mb-2"
                     role="alert"
                     groups="account.group_account_invoice"
                     invisible="not ai_total_mismatch">
                    <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle me-1"
                       role="img" aria-label="Warning" title="Warning"/>
                    <span>The invoice total is</span>
                    <field name="ai_document_total" nolabel="1" readonly="1"
                           class="fw-bold d-inline-block w-auto ms-1"/>
                    <!-- ⚠️ `text-nowrap` on one wrapper per "(tax …)": the
                         bracket was its own inline box, so in a narrow column
                         the line broke between the amount and ")" and the
                         bracket sat alone on the next line (looked at,
                         19.0.3.31.0). One unbreakable group keeps them together. -->
                    <span class="text-nowrap ms-1" invisible="not ai_tax_mismatch">(tax<field
                        name="ai_document_tax" nolabel="1" readonly="1"
                        class="fw-bold d-inline-block w-auto ms-1"/>)</span>
                    <span>; this bill is</span>
                    <field name="amount_total" nolabel="1" readonly="1"
                           class="fw-bold d-inline-block w-auto ms-1"/>
                    <span class="text-nowrap ms-1" invisible="not ai_tax_mismatch">(tax<field
                        name="amount_tax" nolabel="1" readonly="1"
                        class="fw-bold d-inline-block w-auto ms-1"/>)</span>
                    <span>. Review before posting.</span>
                </div>
            </xpath>
        </field>
    </record>
</odoo>
